        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is a fabricated deck worth the extra money?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For thick grass and rough ground, yes. Fabricated decks are welded from heavier steel with deeper geometry that moves more air, which lifts grass for a cleaner cut and disperses clippings better. In our overgrown-grass testing the difference in finish quality was clearly visible. On a flat, well-maintained suburban lawn cut weekly, a stamped deck performs nearly as well.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Should I buy a zero turn mower or a lawn tractor?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Buy a zero turn if your property has trees, beds, and obstacles to mow around, since eliminating trimming passes is where the time savings come from. Buy a lawn tractor if your land is mostly sloped, or if you need one machine that also tows carts, dethatchers, and spreaders — zero turns are poor at towing under load.",
