        <div id="why-zero-turn" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. Zero Turn Mower Buying Guide: Why a Zero Turn Beats a Lawn Tractor
          </h2>

          <p>
            A zero turn mower drives each rear wheel independently, letting it pivot on its own axis instead of swinging through a turning radius. In practice that eliminates the single biggest time waster in mowing: the trimming pass. A lawn tractor leaves an uncut crescent around every tree, post, and bed edge that you then have to go back and clean up. A zero turn wraps the obstacle in one motion.
          </p>

          <p>
            Across our test property, the same two-acre layout took 2 hours 40 minutes on a 42-inch lawn tractor and 55 minutes on a 60-inch zero turn — and the zero turn required almost no follow-up trimming around the eleven trees on the lot. That gap widens with every obstacle. On wide-open acreage with nothing to mow around, the advantage shrinks to deck width and speed alone.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
