          <p>
            The trade-offs are real and worth stating plainly. Zero turns handle slopes worse than tractors because steering comes from the drive wheels — lose traction on a wet hill and you lose steering with it. They are less useful for towing, since the same independent-wheel design that makes them nimble makes them squirrelly under load. And they cost more for equivalent deck width. If your property is mostly hillside or you want one machine for mowing plus hauling, a garden tractor is the better tool.
          </p>
