          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The <strong class="text-white">best zero turn mower</strong> for you comes down to acreage and how long you intend to keep it. For two to five acres, the <strong class="text-white">Toro TITAN MAX</strong> has the components — fabricated deck, serviceable transaxles, greaseable spindles — that decide whether a mower is still cutting well in year ten. For a genuinely strong value, the <strong class="text-white">Ariens IKON XD 52"</strong> delivers a fabricated deck and Kawasaki engine at a residential price. Under two flat acres, the <strong class="text-white">Husqvarna Z254F</strong> is all the mower you need.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever you choose, two habits protect the investment: <strong class="text-white">sharpen blades every 20-25 hours</strong> and <strong class="text-white">respect the 15-degree slope limit</strong>. The first determines how your lawn looks; the second determines whether the machine stays upright.
